1
00:01:43,830 --> 00:01:47,860
[KING OF COMEDY]

2
00:01:48,470 --> 00:01:50,920
[Episode 4]

3
00:01:51,870 --> 00:01:53,280
I'll pay you.

4
00:01:53,870 --> 00:01:54,280
Okay.

5
00:01:54,710 --> 00:01:55,710
You must be tired.

6
00:01:55,950 --> 00:01:56,680
Take a break.

7
00:01:57,310 --> 00:01:57,910
All right.

8
00:01:58,229 --> 00:01:58,870
You too.

9
00:02:00,870 --> 00:02:03,130
It's not like we're demanding to be paid.

10
00:02:03,510 --> 00:02:04,920
Let me think it over.

11
00:02:05,590 --> 00:02:06,920
Let's work on them a little more.

12
00:02:06,920 --> 00:02:08,650
I'll try a different approach.

13
00:02:10,960 --> 00:02:12,690
Weren't you a little too blunt,

14
00:02:12,710 --> 00:02:14,710
bringing up money right off the bat?

15
00:02:14,750 --> 00:02:16,280
Wasn't I telling the truth?

16
00:02:16,420 --> 00:02:17,870
Sure, it's true, but you...

17
00:02:17,870 --> 00:02:19,910
If that's the case,
you should tell her sooner

18
00:02:19,910 --> 00:02:21,310
so she has time to prepare

19
00:02:21,560 --> 00:02:23,560
instead of dragging it out as you do.

20
00:02:25,120 --> 00:02:25,960
But the deadline isn't here yet.

21
00:02:25,960 --> 00:02:26,890
What if it works?

22
00:02:27,510 --> 00:02:29,880
I never really thought
this had a chance.

23
00:02:30,150 --> 00:02:31,800
But things were looking pretty good
the last couple of days.

24
00:02:31,800 --> 00:02:32,530
But today...

25
00:02:33,590 --> 00:02:34,079
Let me tell you.

26
00:02:34,079 --> 00:02:34,960
This job

27
00:02:34,960 --> 00:02:37,190
wasn't worth taking in the first place.

28
00:02:37,630 --> 00:02:39,120
We won't get the job done,

29
00:02:39,120 --> 00:02:40,780
and we won't get paid, either.

30
00:02:42,030 --> 00:02:43,190
She still has to pay us

31
00:02:43,190 --> 00:02:44,120
every last cent.

32
00:02:44,560 --> 00:02:46,360
How about we give them a discount?

33
00:02:46,360 --> 00:02:47,310
What discount?

34
00:02:47,750 --> 00:02:48,480
Discount...

35
00:02:49,560 --> 00:02:50,000
I'm done talking to you.

36
00:02:50,000 --> 00:02:51,400
I've got a call to return.

37
00:02:51,560 --> 00:02:52,280
A debt collector?

38
00:02:52,280 --> 00:02:53,079
Stay out of it.

39
00:02:54,520 --> 00:02:55,520
Let me talk to him.

40
00:02:55,590 --> 00:02:56,310
Stay out of it.

41
00:02:56,310 --> 00:02:57,240
Give me the phone, and I'll talk to him...

42
00:02:57,240 --> 00:02:58,040
Stay out of it!

43
00:03:00,360 --> 00:03:00,870
Hello.

44
00:03:31,430 --> 00:03:32,430
Mr. Chen?

45
00:03:33,340 --> 00:03:35,060
Last time, you said

46
00:03:35,150 --> 00:03:36,030
buying me out...

47
00:03:36,030 --> 00:03:37,630
L-Let's talk about it again.

48
00:03:42,060 --> 00:03:42,780
Mr. Zhou.

49
00:03:43,590 --> 00:03:45,050
I'll let you get back to it.

50
00:04:07,190 --> 00:04:08,390
I've seen you before.

51
00:04:08,710 --> 00:04:10,710
Are you the planner Zhen hired?

52
00:04:10,710 --> 00:04:11,520
What?

53
00:04:11,540 --> 00:04:12,470
I happened to pass by once

54
00:04:12,470 --> 00:04:13,600
and saw you filming.

55
00:04:13,800 --> 00:04:15,590
And you are...

56
00:04:17,510 --> 00:04:18,070
a thief?

57
00:04:19,110 --> 00:04:20,190
Who's a thief?

58
00:04:20,480 --> 00:04:21,339
Let me tell you.

59
00:04:21,480 --> 00:04:23,190
I'm the village chief of this village.

60
00:04:23,190 --> 00:04:24,600
Can a village chief steal?

61
00:04:24,600 --> 00:04:26,600
Could a thief become village chief?

62
00:04:27,040 --> 00:04:28,600
I was hungry.

63
00:04:28,600 --> 00:04:29,720
I wanted some bread.

64
00:04:29,720 --> 00:04:30,720
There was nobody in the store.

65
00:04:30,720 --> 00:04:32,310
So I just grabbed some behind the counter.

66
00:04:32,310 --> 00:04:33,800
Isn't that stealing?

67
00:04:33,800 --> 00:04:34,409
Who's stealing?

68
00:04:34,409 --> 00:04:35,200
Somebody help!

69
00:04:35,200 --> 00:04:35,920
Stop yelling.

70
00:04:35,920 --> 00:04:37,520
If you keep yelling, I'll...

71
00:04:38,600 --> 00:04:39,950
The manager of this shop,

72
00:04:39,950 --> 00:04:41,310
Chen Junnan, is my uncle.

73
00:04:41,310 --> 00:04:42,560
I'm his nephew.

74
00:04:42,560 --> 00:04:44,360
This is our family business.

75
00:04:45,430 --> 00:04:46,310
At your age,

76
00:04:46,310 --> 00:04:48,000
you have the nerve to call him your uncle?

77
00:04:48,000 --> 00:04:49,400
Why not say he's your dad?

78
00:04:50,360 --> 00:04:51,159
Sorry.

79
00:04:51,560 --> 00:04:52,600
I may be old,

80
00:04:52,620 --> 00:04:53,630
but I'm a generation younger than him.

81
00:04:53,630 --> 00:04:54,390
You just make stuff up

82
00:04:54,390 --> 00:04:55,270
and talk nonsense.

83
00:04:55,270 --> 00:04:56,580
At your age... Somebody help!

84
00:04:56,580 --> 00:04:57,920
Someone's robbing the shop!

85
00:04:57,920 --> 00:04:58,800
Dehua. Dehua.

86
00:04:59,240 --> 00:05:00,100
He's stealing.

87
00:05:00,600 --> 00:05:01,410
The village chief's here.

88
00:05:01,410 --> 00:05:02,070
Uncle Dehua,

89
00:05:02,070 --> 00:05:03,530
you're back from fishing?

90
00:05:04,120 --> 00:05:04,630
I'll let you get back to it.

91
00:05:04,630 --> 00:05:05,310
I'm heading home.

92
00:05:05,310 --> 00:05:05,910
All right.

93
00:05:05,920 --> 00:05:07,120
Don't let me keep you.

94
00:05:07,720 --> 00:05:08,450
Uncle Dehua?

95
00:05:08,600 --> 00:05:09,220
See that?

96
00:05:10,630 --> 00:05:12,630
So you really are the village chief?

97
00:05:12,720 --> 00:05:14,720
You wouldn't have guessed, would you?

98
00:05:14,720 --> 00:05:16,270
I didn't realize who I was dealing with.

99
00:05:16,270 --> 00:05:17,630
I-I couldn't see clearly
with my glasses on.

100
00:05:17,630 --> 00:05:18,240
I'm sorry.

101
00:05:18,680 --> 00:05:19,630
My name is Zhou Ke.

102
00:05:19,630 --> 00:05:21,240
I'm making videos for Zhen.

103
00:05:22,070 --> 00:05:23,600
You're young and talented.

104
00:05:24,070 --> 00:05:25,360
I'll keep my glasses on.

105
00:05:25,360 --> 00:05:26,680
I can't handle bright light. (Also implies
someone who's done something shady.)

106
00:05:26,680 --> 00:05:27,740
Can't handle it...

107
00:05:28,750 --> 00:05:29,070
I'm sorry.

108
00:05:29,070 --> 00:05:30,560
Pardon me. Sorry about that.

109
00:05:30,560 --> 00:05:31,560
No, no, not at all.

110
00:05:32,000 --> 00:05:32,600
By the way,

111
00:05:33,490 --> 00:05:35,200
there's something I'd like to ask you.

112
00:05:35,200 --> 00:05:35,830
Go ahead.

113
00:05:35,830 --> 00:05:36,690
Pardon me, too.

114
00:05:36,770 --> 00:05:38,810
From a professional standpoint,

115
00:05:39,600 --> 00:05:42,159
gaining 100,000 followers in 7 days—

116
00:05:42,570 --> 00:05:43,420
is this goal

117
00:05:44,250 --> 00:05:45,050
achievable?

118
00:05:46,720 --> 00:05:48,380
Professionally speaking...

119
00:05:52,270 --> 00:05:53,920
Pardon me for asking, too.

120
00:05:54,310 --> 00:05:58,120
Do you want it to work out or not?

121
00:06:01,100 --> 00:06:02,840
If it works out,

122
00:06:02,870 --> 00:06:05,070
of course I hope it does.

123
00:06:06,000 --> 00:06:07,230
If it doesn't,

124
00:06:09,000 --> 00:06:10,000
that's fine, too.

125
00:06:11,800 --> 00:06:14,130
You've certainly covered all your bases.

126
00:06:16,280 --> 00:06:17,360
No one else is listening here.

127
00:06:17,360 --> 00:06:18,000
Chief,

128
00:06:18,560 --> 00:06:19,760
let me be more direct.

129
00:06:20,390 --> 00:06:21,950
Are you on Zhen's side,

130
00:06:22,120 --> 00:06:23,380
or Chen Junnan's side?

131
00:06:24,750 --> 00:06:26,390
I'm on the villagers' side.

132
00:06:28,600 --> 00:06:29,920
What do you mean?

133
00:06:30,160 --> 00:06:32,600
I can't dictate the villagers' choices.

134
00:06:32,600 --> 00:06:35,190
But I have to give them choices.

135
00:06:35,510 --> 00:06:36,920
That's a very broad perspective.

136
00:06:36,920 --> 00:06:38,920
No wonder you're the village chief.

137
00:06:39,390 --> 00:06:41,580
You said a lot without saying anything.

138
00:06:41,580 --> 00:06:43,440
Those weren't actually my words.

139
00:06:43,560 --> 00:06:45,870
Zhen's father said that.

140
00:06:46,720 --> 00:06:47,190
Her dad?

141
00:06:47,390 --> 00:06:47,870
Yes.

142
00:06:48,120 --> 00:06:50,870
Zhen's dad was the former village chief.

143
00:06:51,120 --> 00:06:53,310
I worked as his accountant back then.

144
00:06:53,870 --> 00:06:54,920
The roads in our village

145
00:06:54,920 --> 00:06:57,390
were all built during his time.

146
00:06:57,630 --> 00:06:58,270
You know?

147
00:07:00,560 --> 00:07:01,560
When he was alive?

148
00:07:01,560 --> 00:07:02,390
Over 10 years ago,

149
00:07:02,390 --> 00:07:03,990
he and his wife went out to sea

150
00:07:04,270 --> 00:07:05,830
and never came back.

151
00:07:09,390 --> 00:07:11,190
Zhen's really had it rough.

152
00:07:11,950 --> 00:07:14,800
She raised Jiahao all by herself

153
00:07:15,560 --> 00:07:16,950
and did everything for him.

154
00:07:16,950 --> 00:07:18,920
She was both a mom and a dad to him.

155
00:07:19,600 --> 00:07:22,270
I get why she's against demolition.

156
00:07:23,160 --> 00:07:25,190
It's not because of the money

157
00:07:25,190 --> 00:07:26,560
she put into renovating the house.

158
00:07:26,560 --> 00:07:28,100
She's afraid that if the house
is demolished

159
00:07:28,100 --> 00:07:30,330
and her parents come back one day,

160
00:07:32,560 --> 00:07:34,620
they won't be able to find their home.

161
00:07:38,000 --> 00:07:38,680
Zhen,

162
00:07:39,190 --> 00:07:41,120
we're going fishing at sea again.

163
00:07:41,740 --> 00:07:43,690
We're going farther out this time.

164
00:07:44,000 --> 00:07:46,120
We might not be back for a week.

165
00:07:46,560 --> 00:07:49,490
When we get back,
I'll make your favorite fish balls.

166
00:07:54,340 --> 00:07:56,710
Zhen, take care of your brother.

167
00:07:58,500 --> 00:08:00,580
He's too simple and trusting.

168
00:08:01,570 --> 00:08:03,100
People can easily fool him.

169
00:08:04,510 --> 00:08:07,170
I've left the money and bankbook
where they are.

170
00:08:07,830 --> 00:08:09,230
Don't tell your brother.

171
00:08:10,190 --> 00:08:11,920
Don't let him handle the money.

172
00:08:13,070 --> 00:08:14,270
We're about to board.

173
00:08:14,960 --> 00:08:18,090
Your mom left enough food for a few days.
Remember to eat.

174
00:08:21,160 --> 00:08:22,390
Nephew of Junnan, please...

175
00:08:22,390 --> 00:08:23,600
please stop crying.

176
00:08:24,870 --> 00:08:25,600
So—

177
00:08:27,240 --> 00:08:28,600
Zhen isn't with you?

178
00:08:31,170 --> 00:08:32,299
No... no, she isn't.

179
00:08:32,429 --> 00:08:34,429
I don't know where she went, either.

180
00:08:37,030 --> 00:08:38,320
Let me tell you a secret.

181
00:08:38,320 --> 00:08:40,049
If you can't find her sometime,

182
00:08:40,600 --> 00:08:43,400
turn left when you leave
and follow the road to the end

183
00:08:43,400 --> 00:08:44,550
until you see a utility pole.

184
00:08:44,550 --> 00:08:46,290
Then turn right and go about a kilometer.

185
00:08:46,290 --> 00:08:48,020
You'll see a lighthouse there.

186
00:08:48,750 --> 00:08:50,200
She goes there whenever she's upset.

187
00:08:50,200 --> 00:08:51,930
You'll find her there for sure.

188
00:09:10,680 --> 00:09:11,920
From up here, our village

189
00:09:11,920 --> 00:09:12,850
is so beautiful.

190
00:09:15,790 --> 00:09:16,270
So beautiful.

191
00:09:16,270 --> 00:09:17,730
How did you know I was here?

192
00:09:18,870 --> 00:09:19,630
I didn't.

193
00:09:20,550 --> 00:09:21,480
I was passing by.

194
00:09:22,180 --> 00:09:24,450
The lighthouse led me here.

195
00:09:26,240 --> 00:09:27,840
I want to be alone for a while.

196
00:09:28,550 --> 00:09:29,080
Okay.

197
00:09:34,670 --> 00:09:36,630
I said I want to be alone for a while.

198
00:09:38,670 --> 00:09:39,080
Woof.

199
00:09:40,150 --> 00:09:41,080
I'm not a person.

200
00:09:50,670 --> 00:09:51,270
It's good.

201
00:09:51,870 --> 00:09:52,730
Cola flavored.

202
00:09:54,600 --> 00:09:55,390
My treat.

203
00:10:03,270 --> 00:10:04,530
Let me tell you a story.

204
00:10:05,510 --> 00:10:06,550
Once upon a time,

205
00:10:07,440 --> 00:10:08,550
there was a kid

206
00:10:09,670 --> 00:10:11,840
who loved acting from a young age.

207
00:10:12,510 --> 00:10:14,480
He could sing and dance.

208
00:10:15,270 --> 00:10:16,440
He could do it all.

209
00:10:17,270 --> 00:10:18,320
He made up his mind

210
00:10:18,790 --> 00:10:21,080
to become a great actor.

211
00:10:23,750 --> 00:10:24,750
But sadly,

212
00:10:26,270 --> 00:10:27,600
he was average-looking

213
00:10:27,870 --> 00:10:29,000
and not tall enough.

214
00:10:30,510 --> 00:10:32,750
His family and friends

215
00:10:33,870 --> 00:10:35,600
thought his dream was a fantasy

216
00:10:36,150 --> 00:10:37,480
and didn't support him.

217
00:10:38,480 --> 00:10:40,340
But he ignored what everyone said

218
00:10:41,440 --> 00:10:42,600
and took the entrance exam

219
00:10:42,600 --> 00:10:44,130
for his dream film academy.

220
00:10:46,150 --> 00:10:47,810
Sure enough, he didn't get in.

221
00:10:48,600 --> 00:10:50,330
But here's the important part.

222
00:10:50,890 --> 00:10:51,890
He didn't give up

223
00:10:52,870 --> 00:10:54,400
retook the exam for 6 years,

224
00:10:56,120 --> 00:10:58,240
and finally got into his dream school.

225
00:10:58,240 --> 00:10:59,900
His dream of acting came true.

226
00:11:01,480 --> 00:11:02,440
And today,

227
00:11:03,080 --> 00:11:04,870
he's become an outstanding,

228
00:11:05,270 --> 00:11:06,320
beloved,

229
00:11:06,790 --> 00:11:08,250
and award-winning actor.

230
00:11:08,550 --> 00:11:10,350
You're an award-winning actor?

231
00:11:11,120 --> 00:11:11,790
I didn't mean me.

232
00:11:11,790 --> 00:11:12,720
I meant Huang Bo.

233
00:11:17,320 --> 00:11:19,440
His story is what inspired me

234
00:11:19,790 --> 00:11:21,870
to work so hard to become an actor.

235
00:11:21,950 --> 00:11:24,240
If I can become an actor,

236
00:11:24,270 --> 00:11:25,730
what can't we accomplish?

237
00:11:25,870 --> 00:11:27,800
I hope his story inspires you, too.

238
00:11:29,960 --> 00:11:30,960
Don't lose heart.

239
00:11:32,130 --> 00:11:34,260
No matter how hard the road ahead gets,

240
00:11:34,600 --> 00:11:36,400
we still have to face it head-on.

241
00:11:37,750 --> 00:11:40,320
We can take mountains
and rivers in stride.

242
00:11:42,000 --> 00:11:43,440
We've still got a few days.

243
00:11:43,440 --> 00:11:45,170
Let's think of something else.

244
00:11:46,390 --> 00:11:47,520
You've still got me.

245
00:11:51,790 --> 00:11:52,600
We can do this.

246
00:11:53,720 --> 00:11:54,720
I've got a feeling

247
00:11:55,030 --> 00:11:55,830
we can do this.

248
00:11:57,200 --> 00:11:59,200
Just look at our beautiful village.

249
00:12:00,030 --> 00:12:00,840
So beautiful.

250
00:12:02,000 --> 00:12:05,840
Good village, good mountains,
good scenery, and good weather.

251
00:12:06,550 --> 00:12:07,340
It's cloudy.

252
00:12:11,440 --> 00:12:12,500
Well, not exactly.

253
00:12:12,910 --> 00:12:15,240
It'll be beautiful when the sun comes out.

254
00:12:15,870 --> 00:12:16,360
Cheers.

255
00:12:18,080 --> 00:12:18,630
Cheers.

256
00:12:22,460 --> 00:12:23,910
See? There it is.

257
00:12:26,560 --> 00:12:28,080
The sun rises as always.

258
00:12:38,460 --> 00:12:40,980
Dad, I know you love
doing crosstalk,

259
00:12:41,360 --> 00:12:42,030
so

260
00:12:42,030 --> 00:12:45,200
I had this custom silk robe
just made for you.

261
00:12:45,790 --> 00:12:46,450
Does it fit?

262
00:12:47,630 --> 00:12:48,960
Isn't it a little tight?

263
00:12:48,960 --> 00:12:49,670
Not at all.

264
00:12:49,670 --> 00:12:51,200
Slim-fit styles are in now.

265
00:12:52,080 --> 00:12:53,360
That's how they dress at DEYUNSHE now.

266
00:12:53,360 --> 00:12:53,840
Really?

267
00:12:53,910 --> 00:12:55,440
Do you know why the collar is open?

268
00:12:55,440 --> 00:12:56,000
Tell me.

269
00:12:56,000 --> 00:12:57,120
So you can warm up your voice.

270
00:12:57,120 --> 00:12:58,200
Oh, enough!

271
00:12:58,630 --> 00:13:00,000
Just admit you bought it too small.

272
00:13:00,000 --> 00:13:01,320
What's with all the bullshit?

273
00:13:01,320 --> 00:13:02,980
You can't get anything right.

274
00:13:03,030 --> 00:13:03,910
Come on, Dad.

275
00:13:04,150 --> 00:13:04,870
Hear me out.

276
00:13:05,600 --> 00:13:06,630
Don't call me Dad.

277
00:13:07,200 --> 00:13:08,790
You divorced Yingying over a year ago.

278
00:13:08,790 --> 00:13:10,840
I'm your former father-in-law at best.

279
00:13:10,840 --> 00:13:12,200
If you couldn't
do crosstalk with me,

280
00:13:12,200 --> 00:13:13,730
I'd have fired you long ago.

281
00:13:14,030 --> 00:13:15,960
Do you know
why I've stayed for over a year?

282
00:13:15,960 --> 00:13:17,550
I want to prove I'm capable

283
00:13:17,550 --> 00:13:18,950
through my own hard work.

284
00:13:19,440 --> 00:13:20,240
You know what?

285
00:13:20,320 --> 00:13:22,440
I really want to get back together
with Yingying.

286
00:13:22,440 --> 00:13:24,200
If you can't get
the Shapu Village job done,

287
00:13:24,200 --> 00:13:25,800
forget about anything else.

288
00:13:26,630 --> 00:13:29,030
If I can't get
the Shapu Village deal done,

289
00:13:29,130 --> 00:13:30,320
I'll resign.

290
00:13:30,780 --> 00:13:33,640
But if I get the Shapu Village
demolition deal done,

291
00:13:34,070 --> 00:13:35,330
put in a good word for me

292
00:13:35,440 --> 00:13:36,700
about me and Yingying.

293
00:13:37,000 --> 00:13:37,600
All right.

294
00:13:38,030 --> 00:13:39,320
What did you just call me?

295
00:13:39,320 --> 00:13:39,870
Dad.

296
00:13:41,510 --> 00:13:43,440
So that's what you were getting at?

297
00:13:45,600 --> 00:13:46,600
Hello, Ms. Haidan.

298
00:13:46,600 --> 00:13:47,200
Zhen.

299
00:13:51,240 --> 00:13:51,840
Mr. Dehua.

300
00:13:51,840 --> 00:13:52,870
Are you going fishing?

301
00:13:52,870 --> 00:13:53,440
Yes, yes.

302
00:13:53,550 --> 00:13:54,610
You're back, Zhen?

303
00:13:56,390 --> 00:13:57,030
Zhen.

304
00:13:57,550 --> 00:13:58,790
I-I want to buy a few things.

305
00:13:58,790 --> 00:13:59,440
You go home first.

306
00:13:59,440 --> 00:14:00,480
Okay. Hurry back.

307
00:14:00,480 --> 00:14:01,000
Okay.

308
00:14:07,440 --> 00:14:08,440
Mr. Chen.

309
00:14:10,150 --> 00:14:11,030
Boss Chen.

310
00:14:12,960 --> 00:14:14,020
Handsome Mr. Chen?

311
00:14:16,200 --> 00:14:19,510
What handsome guy's looking for me?

312
00:14:20,270 --> 00:14:23,630
It's my dear Mr. Zhou.

313
00:14:23,630 --> 00:14:24,830
You're in a good mood.

314
00:14:25,390 --> 00:14:26,080
Mr. Zhou.

315
00:14:34,870 --> 00:14:36,080
Sit, sit, sit.

316
00:14:38,200 --> 00:14:39,060
I just got back.

317
00:14:39,910 --> 00:14:41,710
I came back as soon as you called.

318
00:14:41,840 --> 00:14:42,630
Go ahead.

319
00:14:43,240 --> 00:14:44,570
You've made up your mind

320
00:14:45,120 --> 00:14:46,000
about buying you out?

321
00:14:46,000 --> 00:14:46,840
I have.

322
00:14:48,440 --> 00:14:49,370
I've decided...

323
00:14:51,510 --> 00:14:52,710
I'm turning you down.

324
00:14:57,790 --> 00:14:58,390
Pardon?

325
00:14:59,190 --> 00:15:00,150
I'm turning you down.

326
00:15:00,150 --> 00:15:00,950
Stand up!

327
00:15:08,510 --> 00:15:10,270
I came back as soon as you called.

328
00:15:10,270 --> 00:15:10,600
Yes.

329
00:15:10,600 --> 00:15:11,960
I didn't even get the supplies in town

330
00:15:11,960 --> 00:15:12,600
and came straight back.

331
00:15:12,600 --> 00:15:13,630
I haven't even eaten

332
00:15:13,630 --> 00:15:14,270
or had any water,

333
00:15:14,270 --> 00:15:15,630
and I had to wait, wait, wait...

334
00:15:15,630 --> 00:15:16,550
only to get turned down by you?

335
00:15:16,550 --> 00:15:17,390
Nice dancing.

336
00:15:17,750 --> 00:15:19,410
I wanted to tell you in person.

337
00:15:19,720 --> 00:15:21,050
That's how sincere I am.

338
00:15:21,750 --> 00:15:22,440
It was good?

339
00:15:22,440 --> 00:15:23,030
Yes.

340
00:15:24,840 --> 00:15:26,840
But I don't appreciate the gesture.

341
00:15:27,480 --> 00:15:28,240
What a shame.

342
00:15:28,270 --> 00:15:29,800
Then I'll give you one back.

343
00:15:30,870 --> 00:15:31,400
Get lost.

344
00:15:33,200 --> 00:15:33,730
Goodbye.

345
00:15:34,240 --> 00:15:35,300
Don't regret this.

346
00:15:38,000 --> 00:15:39,330
Regretting it already?

347
00:15:39,440 --> 00:15:40,770
I want to buy some water.

348
00:15:41,150 --> 00:15:41,720
Get lost!

349
00:15:42,440 --> 00:15:42,960
I can't even buy water?

350
00:15:42,960 --> 00:15:44,760
Get lost! I'm not selling to you!

351
00:15:45,200 --> 00:15:46,460
I'm not selling to you!

352
00:16:00,390 --> 00:16:01,000
Ms. Zhen.

353
00:16:03,320 --> 00:16:05,050
W-We still gotta eat, you know.

354
00:16:05,080 --> 00:16:05,510
Right.

355
00:16:05,710 --> 00:16:06,710
Let me get you one.

356
00:16:06,910 --> 00:16:08,600
I'm using the other end
of my chopsticks.

357
00:16:08,600 --> 00:16:10,000
At least have a few bites.

358
00:16:10,870 --> 00:16:11,630
It's okay.

359
00:16:12,270 --> 00:16:14,130
After talking things over today,

360
00:16:14,910 --> 00:16:18,030
I think instead of trying things blindly,

361
00:16:19,320 --> 00:16:21,480
we should go back
to using Yudan and Shengzai.

362
00:16:21,480 --> 00:16:21,790
Right.

363
00:16:21,790 --> 00:16:24,320
Let's think about
how to get them back together.

364
00:16:24,320 --> 00:16:24,790
Right.

365
00:16:25,030 --> 00:16:26,790
They have the best chemistry as a couple.

366
00:16:26,790 --> 00:16:27,910
My cousin keeps telling me

367
00:16:27,910 --> 00:16:29,970
-I really like them.
-she ships them.

368
00:16:30,630 --> 00:16:32,720
Could we try talking Yudan into it?

369
00:16:34,120 --> 00:16:34,720
We already tried.

370
00:16:34,720 --> 00:16:35,150
Right.

371
00:16:36,330 --> 00:16:37,930
Then let's talk to Shengzai.

372
00:16:38,240 --> 00:16:40,100
There's nothing to talk him into.

373
00:16:42,120 --> 00:16:43,180
Then let's do this.

374
00:16:43,320 --> 00:16:44,000
Let's just...

375
00:16:44,000 --> 00:16:44,720
You're close to her.

376
00:16:44,720 --> 00:16:45,670
Let's go tell her.

377
00:16:45,670 --> 00:16:46,630
Their relationship is one thing.

378
00:16:46,630 --> 00:16:47,720
Work is work.

379
00:16:47,720 --> 00:16:48,550
Keep them separate.

380
00:16:48,550 --> 00:16:50,000
Have them put their feelings

381
00:16:50,000 --> 00:16:50,910
aside for now.

382
00:16:50,910 --> 00:16:51,870
Focus on the bigger picture.

383
00:16:51,870 --> 00:16:54,080
Lots of divorced people in show business

384
00:16:54,080 --> 00:16:55,510
still play couples.

385
00:16:55,630 --> 00:16:56,120
It's perfectly normal.

386
00:16:56,120 --> 00:16:57,050
Totally normal.

387
00:16:57,200 --> 00:16:58,270
You're both here.

388
00:16:58,480 --> 00:16:58,960
Jiahao.

389
00:16:59,790 --> 00:17:01,050
You're having dinner?

390
00:17:02,920 --> 00:17:03,790
You made fish balls?

391
00:17:03,790 --> 00:17:05,319
Don't we eat this every day?

392
00:17:11,400 --> 00:17:12,640
Give me 500 yuan.

393
00:17:13,640 --> 00:17:14,400
500?

394
00:17:14,750 --> 00:17:15,550
You're asking me for 500?

395
00:17:15,550 --> 00:17:16,680
Do you know how much money that is?

396
00:17:16,680 --> 00:17:17,940
Are you buying a house?

397
00:17:25,310 --> 00:17:25,920
You two,

398
00:17:25,920 --> 00:17:27,270
could you head upstairs first?

399
00:17:27,270 --> 00:17:27,790
Okay.

400
00:17:29,270 --> 00:17:29,920
Sit down!

401
00:17:32,600 --> 00:17:34,400
What can't you say in front of us?

402
00:17:40,640 --> 00:17:42,270
Obviously, I can't say it
in front of them.

403
00:17:42,270 --> 00:17:42,790
If I could say it,

404
00:17:42,790 --> 00:17:44,270
wouldn't I have said it
as soon as I walked in?

405
00:17:44,270 --> 00:17:45,960
Do you know how much 500 yuan is?

406
00:17:45,960 --> 00:17:47,000
And you're asking me for 500 yuan?

407
00:17:47,000 --> 00:17:47,880
Can you stop lecturing me?

408
00:17:47,880 --> 00:17:49,030
I'm out of options here.

409
00:17:49,030 --> 00:17:50,000
I know He's probably having a hard time.

410
00:17:50,000 --> 00:17:50,640
I'm already...

411
00:17:50,640 --> 00:17:52,590
Do you know how much 500 yuan is?

412
00:17:52,590 --> 00:17:53,960
500 is 5 one-hundreds.

413
00:17:53,960 --> 00:17:55,640
I'm already tearing my hair out!

414
00:17:55,640 --> 00:17:56,880
Do you know how many
fish balls I'd have to sell

415
00:17:56,880 --> 00:17:57,510
I'll say it!

416
00:17:57,510 --> 00:17:58,910
and how long it'd take me—

417
00:17:59,480 --> 00:18:02,480
I was the woman hugging Shengzai
in the sugarcane field!

418
00:18:02,480 --> 00:18:03,160
You?

419
00:18:03,960 --> 00:18:05,400
That person I saw last night was you?

420
00:18:05,400 --> 00:18:06,400
It was me.

421
00:18:07,160 --> 00:18:08,290
Who are you kidding?

422
00:18:08,590 --> 00:18:09,550
It really was me.

423
00:18:10,920 --> 00:18:13,680
I dressed as a woman for a date.

424
00:18:13,750 --> 00:18:15,750
You had to dress as a woman for a date?

425
00:18:15,780 --> 00:18:17,780
The woman I was dating...

426
00:18:18,070 --> 00:18:19,720
is kind of a special person.

427
00:18:20,160 --> 00:18:20,750
Who?

428
00:18:20,770 --> 00:18:21,770
Fang Hua?

429
00:18:23,550 --> 00:18:24,610
What, you know her?

430
00:18:25,160 --> 00:18:25,960
No.

431
00:18:25,960 --> 00:18:27,200
Then why did you freak out like that?

432
00:18:27,200 --> 00:18:27,930
Who is she?

433
00:18:28,000 --> 00:18:29,460
The next village's chief.

434
00:18:31,440 --> 00:18:33,720
I don't care if you're dating the chief

435
00:18:33,750 --> 00:18:35,880
of the next village or our village chief.

436
00:18:35,880 --> 00:18:37,740
Why are you asking me for 500 yuan?

437
00:18:43,750 --> 00:18:44,830
Don't tell me...

438
00:18:49,400 --> 00:18:51,130
We haven't gotten that far yet.

439
00:18:51,880 --> 00:18:54,480
Oh, please.
You'll say anything for Shengzai.

440
00:18:54,920 --> 00:18:56,180
I'm telling the truth.

441
00:18:57,200 --> 00:18:58,860
That woman I saw yesterday...

442
00:18:58,880 --> 00:19:01,740
Her feet were the only thing
that looked like yours.

443
00:19:01,880 --> 00:19:03,160
She had long hair.

444
00:19:03,720 --> 00:19:05,050
Where's your long hair?

445
00:19:16,310 --> 00:19:17,310
Believe me now?

446
00:19:17,880 --> 00:19:19,010
That's disgusting.

447
00:19:19,590 --> 00:19:21,390
You even carry long hair around.

448
00:19:22,550 --> 00:19:24,880
I brought it to explain everything to you.

449
00:19:24,880 --> 00:19:26,480
But she was wearing a red coat, too.

450
00:19:26,480 --> 00:19:27,740
Where's your red coat?

451
00:19:28,790 --> 00:19:30,720
Well, I ran away, remember?

452
00:19:31,110 --> 00:19:32,960
I ran down to the beach

453
00:19:33,550 --> 00:19:34,960
and took it off.

454
00:19:35,000 --> 00:19:35,830
And then...

455
00:19:36,510 --> 00:19:37,880
Suddenly, a gust of wind came

456
00:19:37,880 --> 00:19:38,790
and blew it away.

457
00:19:38,790 --> 00:19:40,350
It blew away?

458
00:19:40,440 --> 00:19:42,070
Yes. It flew away on its own.

459
00:19:43,310 --> 00:19:43,910
Look at me.

460
00:19:44,750 --> 00:19:45,950
I'm flying away, too.

461
00:19:48,000 --> 00:19:49,590
I'm telling the truth.

462
00:19:49,750 --> 00:19:50,590
Then go find the coat.

463
00:19:50,590 --> 00:19:52,450
Why are you asking me for 500 yuan?

464
00:19:52,790 --> 00:19:54,590
Let me finish.

465
00:19:54,640 --> 00:19:56,670
Go on. I love hearing this stuff.

466
00:20:15,030 --> 00:20:15,630
It's mine.

467
00:20:16,160 --> 00:20:16,760
It's mine.

468
00:20:17,270 --> 00:20:17,870
It's mine.

469
00:20:18,200 --> 00:20:18,830
It's mine.

470
00:20:18,960 --> 00:20:20,480
It's mine. It's mine.

471
00:20:21,310 --> 00:20:21,830
500.

472
00:20:22,000 --> 00:20:22,920
I don't have that kind of money.

473
00:20:22,920 --> 00:20:23,920
W-Would 80 work?

474
00:20:25,400 --> 00:20:25,920
500.

475
00:20:27,400 --> 00:20:28,060
Give me 500.

476
00:20:29,400 --> 00:20:30,880
Where'd you get the red coat?

477
00:20:30,880 --> 00:20:31,640
I bought it.

478
00:20:31,880 --> 00:20:32,720
How much?

479
00:20:32,720 --> 00:20:33,550
80.

480
00:20:34,350 --> 00:20:35,750
Where'd you get the money?

481
00:20:35,750 --> 00:20:37,750
I saved up the allowance you gave me.

482
00:20:38,640 --> 00:20:39,440
For 6 months.

483
00:20:40,960 --> 00:20:43,220
I've been stuck eating 50-cent ice pops.

484
00:20:44,030 --> 00:20:45,480
You want 500 from me.

485
00:20:45,680 --> 00:20:46,920
80 for the outfit.

486
00:20:46,920 --> 00:20:48,250
That's 580 altogether.

487
00:20:48,270 --> 00:20:50,000
You made such a mess
of things for Yudan and Shengzai.

488
00:20:50,000 --> 00:20:51,200
And you want 580 from me?

489
00:20:51,200 --> 00:20:52,590
You made this whole mess
just because you wanted to date someone.

490
00:20:52,590 --> 00:20:54,160
You really are good at messing things up.

491
00:20:54,160 --> 00:20:55,440
And you still have the nerve
to ask me for 580?

492
00:20:55,440 --> 00:20:56,680
How do you have the nerve
to ask me for 580?

493
00:20:56,680 --> 00:20:57,790
He didn't do it on purpose. It's okay.

494
00:20:57,790 --> 00:20:58,440
It's not that much money.

495
00:20:58,440 --> 00:20:59,810
We could cover it ourselves.

496
00:20:59,810 --> 00:21:00,240
Right?

497
00:21:03,240 --> 00:21:04,370
Thank you, Mr. Zhou.

498
00:21:04,640 --> 00:21:06,100
It'll come out of your pay.

499
00:21:06,160 --> 00:21:07,000
It's settled.

500
00:21:07,150 --> 00:21:08,280
Thank you, Mr. Zhou.

501
00:21:18,160 --> 00:21:19,400
Believe me now?

502
00:21:19,960 --> 00:21:21,490
You're really disgusting.

503
00:21:27,000 --> 00:21:28,060
What are you doing?

504
00:21:29,780 --> 00:21:31,240
-I'm sorry.
-It wasn't me.

505
00:21:33,680 --> 00:21:34,790
Give me a hug.

506
00:21:36,270 --> 00:21:37,680
I'm sorry.

507
00:21:38,920 --> 00:21:40,560
I know what happened now.

508
00:21:40,640 --> 00:21:42,030
I was innocent.

509
00:21:42,030 --> 00:21:43,790
I was so wronged.

510
00:21:44,270 --> 00:21:45,310
I got violent.

511
00:21:45,880 --> 00:21:47,440
You didn't call the cops, did you?

512
00:21:47,440 --> 00:21:48,200
I almost did.

513
00:21:52,680 --> 00:21:53,280
Oh, right.

514
00:21:53,520 --> 00:21:55,000
I have a gift for you.

515
00:21:57,120 --> 00:21:58,320
A stalk of sugarcane.

516
00:22:00,240 --> 00:22:00,960
Don't...

517
00:22:01,800 --> 00:22:03,400
So many people are watching.

518
00:22:04,770 --> 00:22:06,250
Who's watching us?

519
00:22:06,610 --> 00:22:08,210
It's just us in here isn't it?

520
00:22:13,440 --> 00:22:15,000
Don't give up. Don't give up.

521
00:22:15,000 --> 00:22:16,480
At least we solved one problem.

522
00:22:16,480 --> 00:22:17,830
Even if we can't use the two of them,

523
00:22:17,830 --> 00:22:20,070
at least we didn't cause them any harm.

524
00:22:21,270 --> 00:22:22,530
Let's think of a B plan.

525
00:22:22,720 --> 00:22:24,180
There must be another way.

526
00:22:24,590 --> 00:22:26,000
I have someone in mind.

527
00:22:28,480 --> 00:22:30,240
On the day we held the auditions,

528
00:22:30,240 --> 00:22:32,300
lots of people came for the free eggs.

529
00:22:32,470 --> 00:22:33,480
An old man told me

530
00:22:33,480 --> 00:22:35,440
Yin Tinchiu was based on him.

531
00:22:35,860 --> 00:22:37,240
Sir, go home and wait to hear from us.

532
00:22:37,240 --> 00:22:38,200
Okay. Thank you.

533
00:22:40,560 --> 00:22:41,220
Young lady.

534
00:22:42,070 --> 00:22:43,160
What is this audition for?

535
00:22:43,160 --> 00:22:44,240
"King of Comedy."

536
00:22:44,680 --> 00:22:46,750
Sir, you've got quite a presence.

537
00:22:46,750 --> 00:22:47,830
How about I give you a number

538
00:22:47,830 --> 00:22:48,960
and let you try it too?

539
00:22:48,960 --> 00:22:49,960
"King of Comedy'?

540
00:22:50,440 --> 00:22:51,750
Is it that "King of Comedy"?

541
00:22:51,750 --> 00:22:52,350
Yes.

542
00:22:52,350 --> 00:22:52,920
What other "King of Comedy"

543
00:22:52,920 --> 00:22:53,880
is there?

544
00:22:54,400 --> 00:22:56,000
They didn't get it right back then.

545
00:22:56,000 --> 00:22:57,440
You think you can get it right this time?

546
00:22:57,440 --> 00:22:58,830
W-What do you mean?

547
00:22:59,830 --> 00:23:02,000
He just wouldn't listen to me back then.

548
00:23:02,000 --> 00:23:03,590
That's why it didn't turn out well.

549
00:23:03,590 --> 00:23:04,920
Wouldn't listen to you?

550
00:23:05,000 --> 00:23:07,110
Who? Stephen Chow?

551
00:23:08,960 --> 00:23:09,960
Yeah, young Chow.

552
00:23:10,700 --> 00:23:12,450
The Stephen you're talking about...

553
00:23:12,450 --> 00:23:13,720
He came to our village back then

554
00:23:13,720 --> 00:23:15,690
and lived with me for over a year.

555
00:23:16,100 --> 00:23:17,390
He watched me every day

556
00:23:17,640 --> 00:23:19,310
and based the movie on me.

557
00:23:19,310 --> 00:23:19,880
Me.

558
00:23:21,830 --> 00:23:23,480
So your surname is Yin?

559
00:23:24,750 --> 00:23:25,590
My surname is Chen.

560
00:23:25,590 --> 00:23:26,920
Chen Tinchiu?

561
00:23:27,000 --> 00:23:27,860
Chen Xingwang.

562
00:23:28,160 --> 00:23:29,240
Mr. Xingwang?

563
00:23:33,350 --> 00:23:33,880
What's wrong with you?

564
00:23:33,880 --> 00:23:34,680
Hey, hey, hey.

565
00:23:35,720 --> 00:23:36,550
What are you doing?

566
00:23:36,550 --> 00:23:37,350
What's wrong?

567
00:23:38,000 --> 00:23:38,640
What's going on?

568
00:23:38,640 --> 00:23:39,510
Do you know who he is?

569
00:23:39,510 --> 00:23:40,310
Who?

570
00:23:40,640 --> 00:23:41,790
He's Chen Junnan's dad.

571
00:23:41,790 --> 00:23:43,920
He's obviously here to cause trouble.

572
00:23:44,550 --> 00:23:45,880
He's Chen Junnan's dad?

573
00:23:46,790 --> 00:23:49,790
But my sister says
he inspired the character Yin Tinchiu.

574
00:23:49,790 --> 00:23:50,880
How is that possible?

575
00:23:50,880 --> 00:23:52,400
I've never heard that in my whole life.

576
00:23:52,400 --> 00:23:54,030
It happened before you were born.

577
00:23:54,030 --> 00:23:55,030
What's that supposed to mean?

578
00:23:55,030 --> 00:23:57,030
Let's look at this objectively.

579
00:23:57,640 --> 00:23:59,440
Even if he's Chen Junnan's dad...

580
00:23:59,440 --> 00:24:01,300
That doesn't mean they're alike.

581
00:24:01,790 --> 00:24:02,590
Besides,

582
00:24:02,680 --> 00:24:04,680
we don't have any other options right now.

583
00:24:04,680 --> 00:24:06,140
We're running out of time.

584
00:24:06,270 --> 00:24:09,480
What if he really is
the inspiration for Yin Tinchiu,

585
00:24:10,000 --> 00:24:11,030
I hope he is too,

586
00:24:11,240 --> 00:24:13,240
wouldn't that solve our problem?

587
00:24:14,830 --> 00:24:16,640
Fine. But I don't trust him.

588
00:24:16,640 --> 00:24:17,400
I trust you.

589
00:24:20,790 --> 00:24:21,350
Trust me.

590
00:24:22,310 --> 00:24:22,850
All right.

591
00:24:22,850 --> 00:24:24,070
Let's go in and get to know him a little.

592
00:24:24,070 --> 00:24:24,880
I'm not going.

593
00:24:25,200 --> 00:24:25,750
Why?

594
00:24:26,000 --> 00:24:27,160
He's been saying he wanted me
to marry his son

595
00:24:27,160 --> 00:24:28,220
since I was little.

596
00:24:28,480 --> 00:24:29,960
He's been going on
about it for over 10 years.

597
00:24:29,960 --> 00:24:30,800
I don't want to see him.

598
00:24:30,800 --> 00:24:32,990
Over 10 years? He's persistent.

599
00:24:33,440 --> 00:24:34,480
Then go home.

600
00:24:34,480 --> 00:24:35,540
I'll go talk to him.

601
00:24:35,920 --> 00:24:37,050
Go on. Leave it to me.

602
00:24:43,400 --> 00:24:44,160
Sir.

603
00:24:45,680 --> 00:24:46,720
You're calling me "Sir" again?

604
00:24:46,720 --> 00:24:48,850
That makes me sound old. Call me "bro."

605
00:24:53,550 --> 00:24:54,110
Bro.

606
00:24:54,270 --> 00:24:56,920
You said Yin Tinchiu was based on you?

607
00:24:58,110 --> 00:24:59,350
If I may ask,

608
00:24:59,920 --> 00:25:00,960
you weren't

609
00:25:01,480 --> 00:25:03,510
sent by your son
to cause trouble, were you?

610
00:25:03,510 --> 00:25:04,440
What did you say?

611
00:25:04,680 --> 00:25:06,030
My son caused trouble for you?

612
00:25:06,030 --> 00:25:08,230
He caused a whole lot of trouble.

613
00:25:08,450 --> 00:25:09,490
Pretty Boy.

614
00:25:09,720 --> 00:25:11,550
If you'd told me he was your son,

615
00:25:11,550 --> 00:25:13,880
I wouldn't have added you on social media.

616
00:25:14,310 --> 00:25:15,550
Who's Pretty Boy?

617
00:25:16,070 --> 00:25:17,730
That's his social media name.

618
00:25:18,350 --> 00:25:20,070
Nice. Playful.

619
00:25:20,550 --> 00:25:22,070
I really didn't know about this.

620
00:25:22,070 --> 00:25:23,130
I'll deal with him when I get home.

621
00:25:23,130 --> 00:25:24,830
Could you give him another chance,

622
00:25:24,830 --> 00:25:25,760
Little Dimples?

623
00:25:27,170 --> 00:25:28,430
Who's Little Dimples?

624
00:25:28,480 --> 00:25:29,600
That's my social media name.

625
00:25:29,600 --> 00:25:30,600
I just changed it.

626
00:25:33,960 --> 00:25:35,920
Sir, as for your son...

627
00:25:35,920 --> 00:25:37,270
Go ahead and deal with him.

628
00:25:37,270 --> 00:25:38,960
But you said

629
00:25:38,960 --> 00:25:41,920
"King of Comedy" was based on you.

630
00:25:41,920 --> 00:25:42,680
Well...

631
00:25:43,200 --> 00:25:44,400
You don't believe me?

632
00:25:46,200 --> 00:25:46,790
You don't believe it, either?

633
00:25:46,790 --> 00:25:49,200
I'm on the fence.

634
00:25:49,310 --> 00:25:51,570
So I wasted all afternoon talking to you.

635
00:25:51,600 --> 00:25:52,750
It wasn't a total waste.

636
00:25:52,750 --> 00:25:55,080
It's just that you
kept talking about eggs

637
00:25:55,240 --> 00:25:56,720
the whole time that day.

638
00:25:56,830 --> 00:25:57,960
So I...

639
00:25:58,000 --> 00:25:59,510
Fine. Just wait.

640
00:25:59,770 --> 00:26:01,230
I'll go get you some proof.

641
00:26:01,920 --> 00:26:03,160
Remember to straighten

642
00:26:03,160 --> 00:26:04,000
your son out.

643
00:26:04,030 --> 00:26:04,830
Don't worry.

644
00:26:06,960 --> 00:26:07,750
Pretty Boy.

645
00:26:08,480 --> 00:26:09,590
He sure can spin a yarn.

646
00:26:09,590 --> 00:26:10,450
Are you single?

647
00:26:11,030 --> 00:26:12,230
I've got my eye on you.

648
00:26:12,300 --> 00:26:14,430
Sir, I don't think we'd be a good match.

649
00:26:15,030 --> 00:26:16,160
Don't get the wrong idea, dear.

650
00:26:16,160 --> 00:26:17,310
I don't mean for me.

651
00:26:17,400 --> 00:26:18,790
My son's single, too.

652
00:26:18,870 --> 00:26:21,070
I think you two would be perfect together.

653
00:26:21,070 --> 00:26:21,930
How about this?

654
00:26:22,030 --> 00:26:23,490
Give me your contact info.

655
00:26:23,790 --> 00:26:24,650
I'm Pretty Boy.

656
00:26:24,960 --> 00:26:25,960
It's my social media number.

657
00:26:25,960 --> 00:26:26,590
Take it.

658
00:26:27,030 --> 00:26:28,550
I was pretty impressed
with you in the interview.

659
00:26:28,550 --> 00:26:29,930
You were interviewing me?

660
00:26:29,930 --> 00:26:31,360
[Life Album]

661
00:26:30,010 --> 00:26:31,590
Look. Look.

662
00:26:32,150 --> 00:26:33,110
Take a good look.

663
00:26:36,030 --> 00:26:37,230
That's Stephen Chow.

664
00:26:39,160 --> 00:26:40,350
Young Stephen insisted on a picture.

665
00:26:40,350 --> 00:26:41,790
I didn't even want to pose with him.

666
00:26:41,790 --> 00:26:42,510
Yeah.

667
00:26:42,510 --> 00:26:44,970
You don't look too happy about it.

668
00:26:45,000 --> 00:26:46,480
You look kind of reluctant.

669
00:26:46,480 --> 00:26:47,750
You were so handsome when you were young.

670
00:26:47,750 --> 00:26:48,610
Believe me now?

671
00:26:49,070 --> 00:26:49,590
Well...

672
00:26:51,160 --> 00:26:52,160
Well, bro...

673
00:26:52,960 --> 00:26:55,550
You didn't Photoshop this, did you?

674
00:26:55,830 --> 00:26:57,200
Watch your mouth.

675
00:26:57,200 --> 00:26:59,030
You mean my photo is "P"?
("P" sounds like "crap" in Chinese.)

676
00:26:59,030 --> 00:27:00,430
It's not that kind of "P."

677
00:27:00,480 --> 00:27:01,440
It's, uh...

678
00:27:01,880 --> 00:27:02,540
Never mind.

679
00:27:03,200 --> 00:27:04,000
Bro.

680
00:27:04,440 --> 00:27:05,920
Do you have any other proof?

681
00:27:05,920 --> 00:27:07,850
I figured you might not believe me.

682
00:27:08,310 --> 00:27:09,970
I've got even stronger proof.

683
00:27:10,750 --> 00:27:11,810
This is... This...

684
00:27:12,480 --> 00:27:13,080
This is...

685
00:27:14,310 --> 00:27:16,070
Look. 200 Hong Kong dollars.

686
00:27:16,200 --> 00:27:18,060
Look. Isn't that Hong Kong money?

687
00:27:18,510 --> 00:27:19,550
It really is.

688
00:27:19,550 --> 00:27:21,010
The year. Look at the year.

689
00:27:21,110 --> 00:27:21,970
It's from 1994.

690
00:27:22,830 --> 00:27:23,960
From 1994.

691
00:27:24,830 --> 00:27:25,350
So what?

692
00:27:26,880 --> 00:27:28,010
It's older than you.

693
00:27:28,200 --> 00:27:29,880
Doesn't 1994 tell you something?

694
00:27:29,880 --> 00:27:30,770
-Yes, yes.
-Think about it.

695
00:27:30,770 --> 00:27:31,230
It does.

696
00:27:31,480 --> 00:27:33,000
He stayed at my place for over a year.

697
00:27:33,000 --> 00:27:34,160
Before he left, he asked me

698
00:27:34,160 --> 00:27:35,590
if he could base a character on me

699
00:27:35,590 --> 00:27:37,050
for a script he was writing

700
00:27:37,070 --> 00:27:39,200
and paid me 200 for the rights.

701
00:27:39,550 --> 00:27:40,940
I still haven't spent it.

702
00:27:40,940 --> 00:27:43,450
So you agreed to it for just 200?

703
00:27:43,480 --> 00:27:44,540
And 10 jins of eggs.

704
00:27:44,880 --> 00:27:45,640
I get it.

705
00:27:45,920 --> 00:27:47,480
Eggs really do the trick with you.

706
00:27:47,480 --> 00:27:48,810
They're hard currency.

707
00:27:49,400 --> 00:27:51,590
He also gave me 2 jins of pig ears.

708
00:27:55,090 --> 00:27:56,880
That's quite a generous deal.

709
00:27:56,880 --> 00:27:57,480
It sure is.

710
00:28:00,990 --> 00:28:01,920
What do you think?

711
00:28:01,920 --> 00:28:03,250
Better safe than sorry.

712
00:28:07,400 --> 00:28:09,720
Bro, Yin Tinchiu was based on you.

713
00:28:09,720 --> 00:28:11,480
-Right.
-We didn't recognize a big shot when we saw one.

714
00:28:11,480 --> 00:28:12,880
-We're finally meeting the real deal.
-Our apologies.

715
00:28:12,880 --> 00:28:13,590
Our apologies. Our apologies.

716
00:28:13,590 --> 00:28:15,350
Well, bro...

717
00:28:15,590 --> 00:28:16,350
In that case,

718
00:28:16,350 --> 00:28:17,480
would you be willing

719
00:28:17,680 --> 00:28:18,960
to appear in our video?

720
00:28:18,960 --> 00:28:20,750
We'd like to show people

721
00:28:20,750 --> 00:28:23,350
true story of the man
who inspired Yin Tinchiu.

722
00:28:24,960 --> 00:28:26,440
Well...

723
00:28:29,400 --> 00:28:31,060
We'll give you 10 jins of eggs.

724
00:28:32,350 --> 00:28:33,030
Well...

725
00:28:33,400 --> 00:28:34,600
And 2 jins of pig ears.

726
00:28:35,850 --> 00:28:37,130
Well...

727
00:28:37,550 --> 00:28:38,750
And another 200 yuan.

728
00:28:40,050 --> 00:28:41,310
200 was fine back then.

729
00:28:41,890 --> 00:28:43,060
But not anymore.

730
00:28:45,000 --> 00:28:45,920
Then how much?

731
00:28:46,070 --> 00:28:46,590
2000.

732
00:28:46,590 --> 00:28:47,400
2000 won't do.

733
00:28:47,550 --> 00:28:48,350
4000 minimum.

734
00:28:48,440 --> 00:28:49,400
And no discounts.

735
00:28:49,400 --> 00:28:51,000
Even then, I might not agree.

736
00:28:51,350 --> 00:28:52,750
That's still not enough?

737
00:28:53,830 --> 00:28:55,270
Then how about

738
00:28:55,880 --> 00:28:57,310
I meet your son?

739
00:28:59,110 --> 00:29:00,350
I'm not asking for more money.

740
00:29:00,350 --> 00:29:01,280
Just meet my son.

741
00:29:02,310 --> 00:29:03,070
Deal.

742
00:29:04,720 --> 00:29:06,250
I watched "King of Comedy."

743
00:29:06,310 --> 00:29:07,790
He didn't even invite me
to the premiere.

744
00:29:07,790 --> 00:29:09,070
I watched a recording of it at home.

745
00:29:09,070 --> 00:29:10,310
Was that supposed to be me?

746
00:29:10,310 --> 00:29:11,370
He won the lottery.

747
00:29:12,240 --> 00:29:13,240
It's the jackpot.

748
00:29:14,350 --> 00:29:15,270
His son died.

749
00:29:16,680 --> 00:29:17,880
Watching this is making me

750
00:29:17,880 --> 00:29:18,510
squirm in my seat.

751
00:29:18,510 --> 00:29:19,920
It's absolutely unbearable.

752
00:29:19,920 --> 00:29:21,120
How did you act it out?

753
00:29:21,310 --> 00:29:22,440
You won the lottery.

754
00:29:23,070 --> 00:29:24,070
It's the jackpot.

755
00:29:24,650 --> 00:29:25,580
Your son died.

756
00:29:27,310 --> 00:29:28,440
See the difference?

757
00:29:29,160 --> 00:29:30,890
Your head tilted the other way?

758
00:29:32,640 --> 00:29:33,560
Next part.

759
00:29:41,030 --> 00:29:42,830
I was watering a tree right here.

760
00:29:43,070 --> 00:29:44,480
Young Stephen ran over and said,

761
00:29:44,480 --> 00:29:44,960
"Don't move.

762
00:29:44,960 --> 00:29:46,360
That's such a great pose.

763
00:29:46,720 --> 00:29:47,750
Let me get a shot of you."

764
00:29:47,750 --> 00:29:49,200
I stood here for 4 hours.

765
00:29:49,580 --> 00:29:50,970
4 whole hours!

766
00:29:52,680 --> 00:29:54,340
Then I saw the finished scene.

767
00:29:54,480 --> 00:29:55,960
There was a girl standing
right in front of me.

768
00:29:55,960 --> 00:29:57,240
So I was standing here watering a tree

769
00:29:57,240 --> 00:29:58,830
while he was over here picking up a girl.

770
00:29:58,830 --> 00:29:59,830
Stand here. Don't move.

771
00:29:59,830 --> 00:30:02,090
See how it feels to stand here
for 4 hours.

772
00:30:06,440 --> 00:30:07,270
Hey.

773
00:30:08,110 --> 00:30:09,720
Can I just not work?

774
00:30:11,440 --> 00:30:12,160
No.

775
00:30:13,510 --> 00:30:14,270
Wait...

776
00:30:14,510 --> 00:30:16,030
That's the original line.

777
00:30:16,680 --> 00:30:18,680
But that's not what I said back then.

778
00:30:18,750 --> 00:30:20,010
Young Stephen said...

779
00:30:20,030 --> 00:30:20,830
Stephen Chow.

780
00:30:21,000 --> 00:30:22,440
I mean, Director Chow said

781
00:30:22,440 --> 00:30:24,440
that he felt so relaxed in our village

782
00:30:24,440 --> 00:30:26,200
and didn't even want to go back
to work in Hong Kong.

783
00:30:26,200 --> 00:30:26,800
I told him,

784
00:30:26,960 --> 00:30:28,160
"If you don't go back to work
in Hong Kong,

785
00:30:28,160 --> 00:30:29,100
how will you make money?

786
00:30:29,100 --> 00:30:31,430
If nobody works, how can we make progress?

787
00:30:31,590 --> 00:30:33,440
How can society develop if nobody works?

788
00:30:33,440 --> 00:30:35,720
How will you afford pork head meat?

789
00:30:35,860 --> 00:30:36,510
You know,

790
00:30:36,510 --> 00:30:37,200
back in 1963,

791
00:30:37,200 --> 00:30:38,720
my family finally managed
to buy a pig head,

792
00:30:38,720 --> 00:30:39,720
and I didn't even get an ear."

793
00:30:39,720 --> 00:30:40,310
Mr. Chen hold on...

794
00:30:40,310 --> 00:30:41,550
Let's leave 1963 out of this for now.

795
00:30:41,550 --> 00:30:43,550
Then what do you think would work?

796
00:30:44,480 --> 00:30:45,480
You have to work.

797
00:30:45,590 --> 00:30:46,880
You gotta work when it's time to work.

798
00:30:46,880 --> 00:30:48,550
Work hard. Keep striving.

799
00:30:49,330 --> 00:30:50,530
Good. That's good.

800
00:30:51,010 --> 00:30:56,270
[Clip from the 1999 film King of Comedy]

801
00:30:53,020 --> 00:30:54,260
Work hard!

802
00:30:54,640 --> 00:30:56,400
Keep striving!

803
00:30:56,400 --> 00:30:57,200
Okay. Here we go.

804
00:30:57,200 --> 00:30:59,750
3, 2, 1, action!

805
00:31:02,200 --> 00:31:02,610
No.

806
00:31:03,160 --> 00:31:04,160
I can't yell that.

807
00:31:04,310 --> 00:31:04,880
Why not?

808
00:31:05,160 --> 00:31:07,160
What sane person stands facing the ocean

809
00:31:07,160 --> 00:31:08,650
and yells out their innermost thoughts?

810
00:31:08,650 --> 00:31:10,240
That's how it goes in the original.

811
00:31:10,240 --> 00:31:11,110
Actors these days

812
00:31:11,110 --> 00:31:12,350
are always shouting at mountains

813
00:31:12,350 --> 00:31:13,200
or the ocean.

814
00:31:13,550 --> 00:31:16,400
"Oh, mountains! Oh, ocean!

815
00:31:16,510 --> 00:31:18,030
I want some pork head meat!"

816
00:31:18,030 --> 00:31:19,510
Isn't that guy nuts?

817
00:31:21,240 --> 00:31:22,070
Back then, young Stephen...

818
00:31:22,070 --> 00:31:23,350
I gave him so many good ideas.

819
00:31:23,350 --> 00:31:24,310
He wouldn't use any of them

820
00:31:24,310 --> 00:31:26,570
and had to dig through the trash instead.

821
00:31:26,840 --> 00:31:27,770
It pissed me off.

822
00:31:28,330 --> 00:31:30,070
The more I talk, the madder I get.

823
00:31:30,070 --> 00:31:31,330
My heart can't take it.

824
00:31:31,830 --> 00:31:32,690
I need my pills.

825
00:31:33,440 --> 00:31:34,700
Movies are doomed now.

826
00:31:35,680 --> 00:31:37,030
Mr. Xingwang. Mr. Xingwang.

827
00:31:37,030 --> 00:31:38,070
D-Don't get upset.

828
00:31:38,070 --> 00:31:39,640
-Did you bring your pills?
-Bro.

829
00:31:39,640 --> 00:31:40,350
How about we change the line?

830
00:31:40,350 --> 00:31:41,200
Bro, don't get upset.

831
00:31:41,200 --> 00:31:42,680
You can't shout, "Work hard!"

832
00:31:42,680 --> 00:31:44,000
Get him a bottle of water first.

833
00:31:44,000 --> 00:31:45,130
How about some eggs?

834
00:31:46,030 --> 00:31:47,030
Back then, young Stephen...

835
00:31:47,030 --> 00:31:48,270
I gave him so many good ideas.

836
00:31:48,270 --> 00:31:49,680
He wouldn't use any of them

837
00:31:49,680 --> 00:31:51,310
and had to dig through the trash instead.

838
00:31:51,310 --> 00:31:52,030
Stand here

839
00:31:52,030 --> 00:31:54,490
and see how it feels to stand here
for 4 hours.

840
00:32:01,680 --> 00:32:02,440
Hey.

841
00:32:02,590 --> 00:32:04,030
Can I just not work?

842
00:32:04,160 --> 00:32:04,720
No.

843
00:32:25,110 --> 00:32:26,440
All right. Get up.

844
00:32:28,070 --> 00:32:28,870
Get up. Get up.

845
00:32:37,570 --> 00:32:41,870
[2 Days Left]

846
00:32:41,890 --> 00:32:42,830
Back then, young Stephen...

847
00:32:42,830 --> 00:32:44,030
I gave him so many good ideas.

848
00:32:44,030 --> 00:32:45,070
He wouldn't use any of them

849
00:32:45,070 --> 00:32:46,590
and had to dig through the trash instead.

850
00:32:46,590 --> 00:32:47,400
Hey.

851
00:32:48,640 --> 00:32:49,970
Stand here. Don't move.

852
00:32:50,440 --> 00:32:52,700
See how it feels to stand here
for 4 hours.

853
00:32:55,070 --> 00:32:55,920
Mr. Zhou.

854
00:32:56,830 --> 00:32:57,830
It's been so long.

855
00:32:58,550 --> 00:33:00,680
Why haven't the numbers gone up at all?

856
00:33:00,790 --> 00:33:02,790
With videos like this,

857
00:33:02,960 --> 00:33:04,310
they need time to catch on.

858
00:33:04,310 --> 00:33:05,440
It's a slow process.

859
00:33:05,440 --> 00:33:06,680
Slow?

860
00:33:07,720 --> 00:33:09,920
It feels like nothing's changed at all.

861
00:33:10,030 --> 00:33:10,880
How about

862
00:33:12,010 --> 00:33:13,410
we stop checking for now?

863
00:33:17,720 --> 00:33:19,440
Don't worry.

864
00:33:20,330 --> 00:33:21,800
Videos like this

865
00:33:22,110 --> 00:33:23,640
usually take a little time.

866
00:33:23,640 --> 00:33:24,740
Right. It takes time.

867
00:33:24,740 --> 00:33:25,700
How long?

868
00:33:25,960 --> 00:33:28,070
Sometimes it takes just a few minutes.

869
00:33:28,070 --> 00:33:28,680
Right.

870
00:33:28,720 --> 00:33:29,790
Other times...

871
00:33:30,030 --> 00:33:31,640
Some videos don't take off

872
00:33:31,640 --> 00:33:33,200
until a year or two later.

873
00:33:33,440 --> 00:33:34,300
You never know.

874
00:33:34,790 --> 00:33:35,790
That won't work.

875
00:33:36,400 --> 00:33:38,110
Our deadline is tomorrow.

876
00:33:38,110 --> 00:33:39,480
I-If we still don't
have 100,000 followers,

877
00:33:39,480 --> 00:33:40,350
what do we do?

878
00:33:40,350 --> 00:33:41,880
That's how the algorithm

879
00:33:41,880 --> 00:33:42,640
works.

880
00:33:42,640 --> 00:33:44,550
First, it shows your video
to a small audience.

881
00:33:44,550 --> 00:33:45,750
If enough people watch it,

882
00:33:45,750 --> 00:33:47,190
it gets shown to a larger audience.

883
00:33:47,190 --> 00:33:48,330
If even more people watch it,

884
00:33:48,330 --> 00:33:50,030
it gets pushed to an even larger audience.

885
00:33:50,030 --> 00:33:51,700
Maybe our views

886
00:33:52,160 --> 00:33:53,220
are growing slowly

887
00:33:53,750 --> 00:33:55,280
because no one's watching.

888
00:33:56,720 --> 00:33:57,750
Mr... Mr. Zhou.

889
00:33:58,520 --> 00:34:00,110
Can you think of something?

890
00:34:06,030 --> 00:34:06,690
I've got it.

891
00:34:07,890 --> 00:34:09,889
We should try a different approach.

892
00:34:09,969 --> 00:34:11,699
You could film me, for example.

893
00:34:11,710 --> 00:34:12,190
Well...

894
00:34:12,440 --> 00:34:13,900
You could film me fishing.

895
00:34:13,940 --> 00:34:15,150
A lot of viewers these days

896
00:34:15,150 --> 00:34:17,020
have never seen this kind of rural life.

897
00:34:17,020 --> 00:34:18,480
They might be interested.

898
00:34:21,800 --> 00:34:23,440
I could play a dog.

899
00:34:23,440 --> 00:34:24,840
I often bark back and forth with the dog

900
00:34:24,840 --> 00:34:25,630
at the entrance to our village.

901
00:34:25,630 --> 00:34:28,960
A lot of people can't
even tell which one of us is the real dog.

902
00:34:29,230 --> 00:34:30,420
How about filming me—

903
00:34:30,420 --> 00:34:32,429
You could say I'm the inspiration
for Liu Piaopiao's character.

904
00:34:32,429 --> 00:34:33,480
I could dress up as a woman again.

905
00:34:33,480 --> 00:34:34,710
I've got experience, too.

906
00:34:34,710 --> 00:34:35,710
Nobody could tell last time.

907
00:34:35,710 --> 00:34:36,760
Jiahao. Jiahao.

908
00:34:38,440 --> 00:34:39,960
Let me be honest with you.

909
00:34:40,590 --> 00:34:41,880
In my experience,

910
00:34:42,590 --> 00:34:43,590
if this video

911
00:34:43,960 --> 00:34:46,320
hasn't taken off by now,

912
00:34:47,670 --> 00:34:50,230
it'll be hard for more people

913
00:34:51,360 --> 00:34:52,710
to see it anytime soon.

914
00:34:52,710 --> 00:34:55,230
We might be running out of time.

915
00:35:00,230 --> 00:35:01,110
It'll be tough.

916
00:35:09,000 --> 00:35:10,060
Where are you going?

917
00:35:10,060 --> 00:35:10,710
I'm going to see the village chief

918
00:35:10,710 --> 00:35:12,190
and ask him for a few more days.

919
00:35:12,190 --> 00:35:13,120
I'll go with you.

920
00:35:13,280 --> 00:35:14,210
You two,

921
00:35:14,360 --> 00:35:15,440
could you wait a few more days?

922
00:35:15,440 --> 00:35:17,510
We'll go talk to the village chief
about it.

923
00:35:17,510 --> 00:35:17,960
Is that okay?

924
00:35:17,960 --> 00:35:18,990
Just wait a few more days.

925
00:35:18,990 --> 00:35:19,800
I think that's fine.

926
00:35:19,800 --> 00:35:21,070
We can stay a few more days.

927
00:35:21,070 --> 00:35:22,960
We'll draw up an additional agreement

928
00:35:22,960 --> 00:35:25,370
and charge separately
for the extra days.

929
00:35:25,440 --> 00:35:26,250
Then we'll...

930
00:35:26,360 --> 00:35:27,620
Please sit down first.

931
00:35:28,510 --> 00:35:29,710
Both of you, sit down.

932
00:35:30,070 --> 00:35:31,360
You sit down first.

933
00:35:33,400 --> 00:35:34,480
Don't worry.

934
00:35:35,190 --> 00:35:36,420
Well, we are worried.

935
00:35:37,880 --> 00:35:39,040
This isn't about the money.

936
00:35:39,040 --> 00:35:40,590
We can even waive our fee.

937
00:35:40,620 --> 00:35:42,060
Don't waive the fee.

938
00:35:42,840 --> 00:35:43,630
No, I mean...

939
00:35:43,800 --> 00:35:45,660
This is really important to them.

940
00:35:45,800 --> 00:35:47,440
This concerns your village

941
00:35:47,550 --> 00:35:49,030
and your house.

942
00:35:51,910 --> 00:35:53,630
I don't want to waste your time.

943
00:35:53,630 --> 00:35:55,670
Even if you get 10 more days,

944
00:35:56,230 --> 00:35:58,800
it probably won't make much difference.

945
00:36:00,030 --> 00:36:00,940
So,

946
00:36:03,030 --> 00:36:04,190
maybe you should

947
00:36:06,130 --> 00:36:07,130
find someone else

948
00:36:07,400 --> 00:36:08,530
and try another way.

949
00:36:11,740 --> 00:36:12,570
I'm sorry.

950
00:36:19,190 --> 00:36:22,030
We're screwed.

951
00:36:22,790 --> 00:36:25,020
Jiahao, stop crying, stop crying.

952
00:36:38,030 --> 00:36:38,630
Dad.

953
00:36:39,840 --> 00:36:41,300
Stop looking at yourself.

954
00:36:41,920 --> 00:36:42,760
Look at me.

955
00:36:43,290 --> 00:36:44,620
What's there to look at?

956
00:36:45,650 --> 00:36:47,380
Why are you making trouble?

957
00:36:48,290 --> 00:36:48,770
Dad.

958
00:36:49,590 --> 00:36:52,280
I-I'm at a crucial stage
in my career right now.

959
00:36:52,360 --> 00:36:53,440
You won't help me,

960
00:36:53,630 --> 00:36:54,710
but them?

961
00:36:57,440 --> 00:36:59,040
Who else would I help but you?

962
00:36:59,920 --> 00:37:00,880
If I weren't helping you,

963
00:37:00,880 --> 00:37:03,140
would she agree to marry into our family?

964
00:37:08,070 --> 00:37:09,400
She agreed?

965
00:37:10,230 --> 00:37:11,890
It's pretty much a sure thing.

966
00:37:12,070 --> 00:37:13,960
The rest is up to you,
so you'd better hurry.

967
00:37:13,960 --> 00:37:14,440
Don't worry.

968
00:37:14,440 --> 00:37:15,630
If she goes back to the Northeast,

969
00:37:15,630 --> 00:37:16,500
it'll be too late.

970
00:37:16,500 --> 00:37:18,100
Going back to the Northeast?

971
00:37:18,920 --> 00:37:19,710
Who?

972
00:37:20,280 --> 00:37:21,360
That chubby girl.

973
00:37:23,480 --> 00:37:23,880
I...

974
00:37:24,230 --> 00:37:26,000
I like Zhen.

975
00:37:26,000 --> 00:37:27,030
Zhen.

976
00:37:28,000 --> 00:37:29,110
What kind of taste do you have?

977
00:37:29,110 --> 00:37:30,480
Zhen's no good for you.

978
00:37:31,070 --> 00:37:31,960
Zhen

979
00:37:32,030 --> 00:37:34,070
is always with that planner guy.

980
00:37:34,550 --> 00:37:35,880
Feelings grow over time.

981
00:37:35,880 --> 00:37:37,590
Sooner or later, they'll get together.

982
00:37:37,590 --> 00:37:39,110
And you'll be heartbroken.

983
00:37:39,110 --> 00:37:39,920
Listen to me.

984
00:37:40,550 --> 00:37:42,800
That girl from the Northeast
is a great catch.

985
00:37:42,800 --> 00:37:44,030
She bought me eggs

986
00:37:44,030 --> 00:37:45,150
and pig ears.

987
00:37:45,150 --> 00:37:46,950
Then I'll buy you some too, okay?

988
00:37:47,360 --> 00:37:48,490
Just stop meddling.

989
00:37:49,320 --> 00:37:51,580
Or I won't know
how to answer to Mr. Huang.

990
00:37:51,840 --> 00:37:53,170
You can't answer to him?

991
00:37:54,580 --> 00:37:56,980
Then how am I supposed
to answer to your mom?

992
00:37:58,800 --> 00:37:59,840
Before she passed away,

993
00:37:59,840 --> 00:38:00,920
she told me

994
00:38:00,920 --> 00:38:01,440
Dad.

995
00:38:01,440 --> 00:38:03,570
to get you married as soon as possible.

996
00:38:05,230 --> 00:38:06,670
I know, I know, I know.

997
00:38:06,670 --> 00:38:07,150
I, I...

998
00:38:07,410 --> 00:38:08,870
I'm leaving, I'm leaving.

999
00:38:17,440 --> 00:38:18,590
When you cover your face,

1000
00:38:18,590 --> 00:38:21,170
you can't tell
whether they're laughing or crying.

1001
00:38:21,170 --> 00:38:22,780
You think I can't handle you?

1002
00:38:24,140 --> 00:38:25,100
You little punk.

1003
00:38:26,500 --> 00:38:28,020
Mr. Zhou, Ms. Lin.

1004
00:38:28,630 --> 00:38:29,870
Thank you for your hard work.

1005
00:38:29,870 --> 00:38:31,670
Thanks for coming to our village
to help us.

1006
00:38:31,670 --> 00:38:32,840
Don't mention it.

1007
00:38:32,960 --> 00:38:34,800
Even though things didn't work out,

1008
00:38:34,800 --> 00:38:36,070
you still deserve credit
for all your hard work.

1009
00:38:36,070 --> 00:38:36,960
It's nothing. We're happy to help.

1010
00:38:36,960 --> 00:38:38,620
I'll pay you what we agreed on.

1011
00:38:38,960 --> 00:38:40,000
Oh, come on.

1012
00:38:40,320 --> 00:38:41,440
You're too kind.

1013
00:38:42,000 --> 00:38:43,190
We didn't come all this way just to...

1014
00:38:43,190 --> 00:38:44,510
Why don't you take it?

1015
00:38:46,060 --> 00:38:46,630
Me?

1016
00:38:46,630 --> 00:38:47,840
Yes. She's transferring it to you,

1017
00:38:47,840 --> 00:38:48,960
not me.

1018
00:38:50,510 --> 00:38:51,590
We didn't manage to help.
